table dialogue id npc:text point:ref.point quest:opt.quest line:text
1|Warden|15|1|The wolves grow bold on the south road. A lone one dens beside it. Put it down and come back to me.
2|Warden|15|2|Goblins have made a camp past the far woods. Find it and drive them off.
3|Warden|15|3|Well done. More of them hunt further south. Walk the road to the overlook above the thicket, then come back whole.
4|Warden|15|4|So a pair holds the thicket. They fight as one. Take them both.
5|Warden|15|5|Three more den in the hollow beyond the thicket. Thin them and bring me a pelt.
6|Warden|15|0|The road is ours again. You have my thanks.
